# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Runtime artefacts
*.log
*.sock

# 🔴 No credential file belongs in this tree under any name. The broker reads
# its keys from a root-owned EnvironmentFile supplied by systemd, never from
# the repo. These patterns are a backstop, not the control -- the control is
# that nothing here ever writes one.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets.json
upstreams.local.json

# 🔴 A FILLED-IN IMPORT FILE IS A CREDENTIAL FILE. keys.example.txt holds only
# placeholders and is committed deliberately; every other key-shaped name here
# is refused. The real control is that the working copy belongs outside this
# tree at mode 600 and gets shredded after import -- this is the backstop.
keys.txt
aj-keys.txt
*-keys.txt
keys.*.txt
!keys.example.txt

# 🔴 EDITOR ARTEFACTS. A .swp / .swo holds the buffer contents of whatever is
# open, so an editor sitting on a filled-in key file puts those bytes on disk
# under a name nothing else was guarding. `git add -A` swept one of these in
# once; these patterns are why it cannot happen again.
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.*.swp
.*.swo
